@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@
+commit 6dedf3410ee40e3d1d7ff58a22499d8ba749fe89
+Author:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
+AuthorDate: Sun Oct 4 00:19:39 2026 -0500
+Commit:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
+CommitDate: Sun Oct 4 00:19:39 2026 -0500
+
+    docs: document event --no-tick-write (DOC-21)
+    
+    README.md and skills/boardctl-usage/SKILL.md omitted the event
+    subcommand's --no-tick-write flag. Add it to both:
+    
+    - README quickstart: --tick N now stated as also rewriting the header
+      ticks_total to max(old, N) (topology A: board.jsonl line 1; legacy
+      topology B: line 1 of tasks.jsonl) with the stderr notice; a
+      --no-tick-write example showing the opt-out and the doctor drift-check
+      consequence.
+    - README behavior section (BT-041 area): full paragraph on the default
+      header bump (max semantics, stderr notice) and the opt-out
+      (byte-identical board file, event row still carries tick_number,
+      per-invocation, doctor FAILs with "ticks_total < max events
+      tick_number" + fix hint while the header lags).
+    - SKILL.md: same content in the Proven commands table and a new
+      Write-vocabularies bullet.
+    
+    Behavior verified live against scratch boards (built binary):
+    default --tick 3 rewrote ticks_total 0 -> 3 with the stderr notice;
+    a later --tick 2 left the counter at 3 (max, never rewinds);
+    --tick 7 --no-tick-write appended the event (tick_number 7 present)
+    and left the header byte-identical; doctor then FAILED with
+    "header ticks_total 0 < max events tick_number 7" + fix hint.
